s.t:
Support month-end and year-end close activities, ensuring financial data accuracy and compliance with Experian accounting policies and IFRS;
Ensure adherence to local statutory, regulatory, and compliance requirements;
Maintain selected balance sheet accounts, including reconciliations, analysis, and resolution of outstanding items;
Help prepare forecasts and financial plans;
Prepare regular and ad hoc financial and management reports to support business decision-making;
Support the planning and control of annual budgets within the assigned region or function;
Partner with other teams to identify opportunities for cost optimization, operational efficiencies, and value creation;
Contribute to process improvements, driving efficiency, standardization, and continuous improvement projects;

1+ year of experience in Finance, Accounting, FP&A, Reporting, Audit, or a related area;
Bachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, or a related field;
Experience with financial statements and accounting principles;
Proficiency in Microsoft Excel; experience with financial systems;
Fluency in English.
